"""The gear hash tables for content-defined chunking -- GENERATED, do not edit.

Eight tables of 256 64-bit values, laid out as eight consecutive runs of 256,
so run `r` byte `b` is index `r * 256 + b`.

Produced by, for seed in 0..7 and n in 0..255:

    md5(bytes([seed] * 64 + [n] * 64)).hexdigest()[:16]

The values only need a uniform distribution; what matters is that they are
*these* values. Arrow C++ (`parquet/chunker_internal_generated.h`) and arrow-rs
(`column/chunker/cdc_generated.rs`) emit byte-identical tables, and marrow's
chunk boundaries deduplicate against their output only while all three agree.
Regenerating this file would silently break that against every file already
written, which is why no generator ships with it -- `test_gearhash_table_intact`
pins it instead.
"""

